      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasant_valley_cdp_new_york",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wappinger Creek, a tributary of the Hudson River, flows through the center of Pleasant Valley, creating a small riparian habitat that supports brook trout and herons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
